"No man can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or else he will hold to the one, and despise the other. We can't serve God and money. 

This verse was chosen as a reminder to serve God. Understand him through his word and obey his clear commands


A few thinga to double click on here

Verse 19: Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth, where moth and rust doth corrupt, and where thieves break through and steal

At the time when the Bible was written,the treasures of eastern kings would have been fine cloth, polished armour and weapons of war as well as gold.

Moth and rust would have been enemies from within and just as threatening as thieves, enemies from without


Last line of verse 24 uses mammon instead of money

Mammon here refers to riches and treasures which are the idols of carnal hearts, set up in opposition to God. Carnal meaning earthly or fleshly, in constrast to heavenly or spiritually







